<%# The three palettes, as three pressed-once buttons rather than a select: a
    theme is a thing to look at, and a menu hides two thirds of the choice
    behind a click. Each button carries its own two colours, so the control
    shows what it will do before it is pressed.

    Drawn without a caption: it sits in the settings page beside a field label
    that already says "Tema", and a second tiny caption in the same row would
    be the same word twice.

    `aria-pressed` is the state, and it is the only thing the script changes
    besides the `data-theme` on <html> — the dots are pure CSS on that same
    attribute, so the labels cannot drift out of step with the page. -%>
<div class="theme-picker" role="group" aria-label="<%= h(I18n.t("web.settings.appearance.theme")) %>">
  <button type="button" class="theme-swatch" data-theme-choice="everforest"
          aria-pressed="false" title="<%= h(I18n.t("web.theme.everforest_title")) %>">
    <span class="swatch-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><%= h(I18n.t("web.theme.everforest")) %>
  </button>
  <button type="button" class="theme-swatch" data-theme-choice="dark"
          aria-pressed="false" title="<%= h(I18n.t("web.theme.dark_title")) %>">
    <span class="swatch-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><%= h(I18n.t("web.theme.dark")) %>
  </button>
  <button type="button" class="theme-swatch" data-theme-choice="light"
          aria-pressed="false" title="<%= h(I18n.t("web.theme.light")) %>">
    <span class="swatch-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><%= h(I18n.t("web.theme.light")) %>
  </button>
</div>
